    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You know that the core concept of dynamic programming is to divide the problem into smaller subproblems i.e., a series of decision steps."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So what might be the decision step for our knapsack problem?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The simplest decision step is to check whether you want to add the item to the bag or not."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So, we'll be using the decision trees we learned in the Binary Trees chapter."
    },
